[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it describe
three different problems. Fixing the parser closes only the first; the other two keep coming in
under the same subjects.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not touch <code>hint</code> or <code>one-day-move</code>. Each has its own
ticket now. Keep #4471 for <code>parser</code> only.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: day-first dates read month first.** The shared parser reads every date month first.
For a tenant whose locale writes the day first, day and month swap: 6 May becomes 5 June. Every
channel, every tenant on file.

**`hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type month first.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
its date field, and then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint
says. Only the form channel, only the tenants that run booking-v3. The parser fix leaves it as is.

**`one-day-move`: the date moves by one day.** These reports are not a swap: the date lands one
day early or late, or two people at the same meeting get different days ("Client in Lisbon got
Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). The desk already read them that way
(`desk-notes.json`), and the #4471 page still files them under `parser` by tenant. A day/month
swap cannot move a date by one day, so this is a time zone or day-boundary bug.

## How the merge hid them

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. The same
  subjects come in for all three problems, so all three ended in one ticket. The cause depends on
  the tenant and the way in (`causes.ts`), not on the subject.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant's cause in
  both directions. The table counts by cause, not by tag.
- The ticket export overlaps between pages, so some reports come twice. Each id is counted once.

## What to change

- Engineering: one fix per ticket above. The `hint` fix is in booking-v3's date hint, not in the parser.
- Desk: a new decision record that merges on cause (tenant, form, channel) instead of subject.
  0001 stays as it is; the new record replaces it.

